    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Competitive exams frequently ask about the minimum number of Whole-Time Members (WTMs): out of 5 appointed members, at least 3 must be whole-time members.",
        "Note the nominating bodies: RBI nominates 1 member, Union Finance Ministry nominates 2 members, and the Central Government appoints the Chairman and remaining 5 members.",
        "Total statutory composition consists of 9 members under Section 4 of the SEBI Act, 1992."
      ],
      "id": "10dh5fm"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The SEBI Board is constituted under Section 4 of the Securities and Exchange Board of India Act, 1992.",
        "The Chairman of the Board is appointed directly by the Central Government of India.",
        "Two members are nominated from amongst the officials of the Union Ministry of Finance.",
        "One member is nominated by the Reserve Bank of India (RBI).",
        "Five other members are appointed by the Central Government, out of which at least three must be whole-time members."
      ],
      "id": "tsw5xko"
